---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import HeroDemo from '../components/HeroDemo.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import FeatureRow from '../components/FeatureRow.astro';
import CompareTable from '../components/CompareTable.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import { HOME_FEATURES, HOME_MORE } from '../data/content';
import { LINKS, INSTALL_CMD } from '../data/site';
import { getReleases } from '../lib/changelog';

const [latest] = await getReleases();
const agentCmd = 'curl -fsSL "https://<your-server>/install/agent.sh?token=…" | sudo bash';
const composeSnippet = 'services:\n  app:\n    image: ghcr.io/you/app:1.4\n    ports:\n      - "8080:80"';
const hosts: [string, number, number][] = [['home-nas · behind NAT', 14, 20], ['vps-frankfurt', 80, 16], ['office-pi', 12, 80], ['customer-01 · firewall', 82, 82]];
---
<Base title="Dockmesh" description="Manage Docker Compose stacks on all your hosts from one web UI. One binary, outbound-only agents, free and open source with every feature included." searchKind="Website">
  <section class="hero">
    <canvas class="mesh" id="mesh" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="dm-wrap hero-in">
      <a class="eyebrow" href={`/changelog/${latest.version}/`}><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>v{latest.version} is out · read the release notes <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <h1>Every Docker host.<br /><em>One place.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Deploy, back up and publish your compose stacks across all your servers from one web interface. Free and open source, with every feature included — no paid tier, no node limit.</p>
      <div class="cta-row"><a class="dm-btn pri lg" href={LINKS.install}>Install in five minutes</a><a class="dm-btn lg" href={LINKS.github}>View on GitHub</a></div>
      <CodeBlock code={INSTALL_CMD} lang="bash" class="hero-install" />
      <HeroDemo />
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="dm-wrap"><div class="trust">
    <div><b>Tested on real machines</b><span>Releases are tried on a lab of real VMs — server, agents and a backup host — before they are tagged, including upgrades from the previous release. Backup targets are also tested in CI against real SMB, SFTP, WebDAV and S3 servers.</span></div>
    <div><b>Security in the open</b><span>Fixes ship with published advisories, and problems can be reported privately on GitHub.</span><a href={LINKS.security}>Advisories →</a></div>
    <div><b>Every change written down</b><span>A public changelog says what changed and whether to update right away.</span><a href="/changelog/">Changelog →</a></div>
    <div><b>Free, for good</b><span>AGPL-3.0. Roles, single sign-on and the audit log are in the open code.</span><a href="/about/">Why it's free →</a></div>
  </div></div>

  <section class="sec"><div class="dm-wrap">
    <div class="sechead"><p class="kicker">How it works</p><h2>Running in three steps.</h2></div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div><span class="n">1</span><h3>Install the server</h3><CodeBlock code={INSTALL_CMD} lang="bash" /><p>On a Linux host with Docker. The setup wizard opens in your browser.</p></div>
      <div><span class="n">2</span><h3>Add your other hosts</h3><CodeBlock code={agentCmd} lang="bash" /><p>Hosts → Add host shows the exact command. The agent connects out to the server; no port to open on the host.</p></div>
      <div><span class="n">3</span><h3>Deploy a stack</h3><CodeBlock code={composeSnippet} lang="yaml" /><p>Paste a compose file, pick a template, or adopt the Compose projects already running.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="sec band"><div class="dm-wrap">
    <div class="sechead"><p class="kicker">What it does</p><h2>Built around the questions you actually have.</h2></div>
    <div>{HOME_FEATURES.map((f, i) => <FeatureRow f={f} rev={i % 2 === 1} />)}</div>
    <div class="more">{HOME_MORE.map(([b, s]) => <div><b>{b}</b><span>{s}</span></div>)}</div>
    <p style="margin-top:26px"><a class="arrow-link" href="/features/">All features <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="sec"><div class="dm-wrap dialwrap">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">How remote hosts connect</p>
      <h2>No open port on your remote hosts.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Most managers dial into each host, so every host needs an open port, a fixed address or a VPN. Dockmesh agents dial out to the server instead, over mutual TLS on one port of the server (8443 by default).</p>
      <ul class="checks"><li>Works behind NAT and firewalls you don't control</li><li>Each agent proves itself with its own certificate</li><li>Remove a host and its connection ends</li></ul>
      <p style="margin-top:20px"><a class="arrow-link" href="/docs/concepts/hosts-and-agents/">How agents connect <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="meshpanel">
      <canvas id="mesh2" role="img" aria-label="Diagram: four remote hosts connect out to the Dockmesh server"></canvas>
      <div class="mlabels" aria-hidden="true"><span style="left:50%;top:50%" class="srv">Dockmesh server</span>{hosts.map(([n, x, y]) => <span style={`left:${x}%;top:${y}%`}>{n}</span>)}</div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="sec band"><div class="dm-wrap">
    <div class="sechead"><p class="kicker">Compared</p><h2>What others charge for, Dockmesh ships for free.</h2><p class="lede">Six rows where the difference shows. The full comparison also lists what the alternatives do better.</p></div>
    <CompareTable landing />
    <p style="margin-top:22px"><a class="arrow-link" href="/compare/">Full comparison <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="sec"><div class="dm-wrap" style="max-width:860px">
    <div class="sechead"><p class="kicker">FAQ</p><h2>Questions people actually ask.</h2></div>
    <Faq limit={5} />
    <p style="margin-top:22px"><a class="arrow-link" href="/about/">About the project <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="sec final"><div class="dm-wrap closing">
    <div><h2>Try it on one host tonight.</h2><p class="lede" style="margin-top:10px">One command on a Linux machine with Docker. If it isn't for you, remove it — your compose files stay where they are.</p></div>
    <div class="cta-row" style="margin:0"><a class="dm-btn pri lg" href={LINKS.install}>Install Dockmesh</a></div>
  </div></section>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .hero { position: relative; overflow: hidden; padding: 64px 0 56px; }
  .hero .mesh { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 760px; pointer-events: none; -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 55% 60% at 80% 30%, #000 25%, transparent 75%); mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 55% 60% at 80% 30%, #000 25%, transparent 75%); }
  .hero-in { position: relative; }
  @media (max-width: 980px) { .hero .mesh { display: none; } }
  .hero h1 em { font-style: normal; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero-install { max-width: 560px; margin-top: 22px; }
  .eyebrow { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border2); background: var(--surface); border-radius: 999px; padding: 4px 12px 4px 10px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 22px; transition: border-color 0.15s; }
  .eyebrow:hover { border-color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .eyebrow .dot { width: 7px; height: 7px; background: var(--ok); border-radius: 50%; }
</style>

<script>
  import { mesh } from '../scripts/mesh';
  mesh(document.getElementById('mesh') as HTMLCanvasElement, { count: 20, center: [0.8, 0.3], alpha: 0.5, seed: 11, every: 380, hub: 120, hubBg: '--bg' });
  mesh(document.getElementById('mesh2') as HTMLCanvasElement, { nodes: [[0.14, 0.2], [0.8, 0.16], [0.12, 0.8], [0.82, 0.82], [0.32, 0.12], [0.66, 0.9], [0.92, 0.48], [0.06, 0.5]], every: 600, hub: 130 });
</script>
